      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Interesting. yt-dlp gets a link to an mp4 file from youtube with audio and video in the same format, and for 720p its 30fps. \n\n22  mp4   1280x720    30  2 | 112.86MiB   376k https | avc1.64001F          mp4a.40.2       44k [en] 720p\n\nIf you take a look at a 30fps format like 480p you will see this issue in a browser. So this is not a VRChat bug. \n\nFor anyone else looking at this, the t=76 is 1:16 into the video and a good place to see the neutral zone flickering. In the intro the stuff in the middle flickers and then is stabilized while the narrator is talking about the neutral zone concept",
